Privacy Policy for Tab Wallet

Last updated: November 2026

Tab Wallet is a lightweight, privacy-first Chrome extension designed to help users save, manage, and restore tab sessions, allowing them to free up system RAM efficiently.

1. Data Collection
Tab Wallet does NOT collect, store, process, or transmit any personal data, browsing history, URLs, or user information to external servers. All operations, including the creation, storage, and restoration of tab sessions, are performed and saved entirely locally on your device using Chrome's local storage.

2. Use of Permissions
Tab Wallet requests the absolute minimum permissions necessary to function. Here is exactly how each permission is used:

- tabs: Used solely to query the URLs and titles of open tabs in the current window to save them into a session, and to close those specific tabs upon explicit user request to free up RAM. We do NOT read, track, modify, or log the content of your tabs, nor do we monitor your browsing history.

- storage: Used exclusively to save and load your custom tab sessions ('sessions' array) locally on your device via chrome.storage.local. This data never leaves your browser.

- favicon: Used strictly to fetch and display the standard website icons (favicons) next to the saved URLs in the extension popup for better visual recognition. This utilizes Chrome's built-in, local favicon service.

3. Third-Party Sharing
We do not share any data with third parties, as no data is collected or transmitted outside of your local browser environment.
